    {
      "title": "γδ T cell receptor dependencies define a unique immunosurveillance modality",
      "link": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-11076-4",
      "description": "<p>Nature, Published online: 30 September 2026; <a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-11076-4\">doi:10.1038/s41586-026-11076-4</a></p>Tissue-resident γδ T cells mount rapid, innate-like stress responses that require γδ T cell receptor signalling, revealing lineage-specific receptor dependence that underpins their conserved roles in immunosurveillance and informs therapeutic deployment.",
